      "id": "CHANNEL4-GLOBAL-ORIGINAL-ID-LEDGER-1",
      "lines": [
        410,
        427
      ],
      "mechanism": "Each packet can pass current-state and per-query/per-cursor base ledgers while conflicting only with a candidate exposed earlier by another query/cursor. The global _observe loop compares only outer decorated IDs. Distinct base preimages can have distinct decorated IDs even if their original prototype IDs collide; full original collision provenance must remain checked without assuming hash injectivity.",
      "minimal_repair": "Preserve v10; compare incoming nested base_tile.placement_key ID/fullpreimage with every existing observed nested base key in the same global _observe loop, alongside unchanged outer comparison. Use same COW observed structure and rollback, no new cache/scheduler restriction.",
      "scope": "A Source-level fail-closed identity/conformance defect; no collision occurrence, scientific execution, runtime result or invalid accepted proof is asserted.",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "summary": "Global observed ledger omits nested original base prototype IDs/preimages across different query/cursor packets."
    }
  ],
  "disclosure": "Reviewer authored original membership/c960/fallback and current point decorator, plus engine9 marking-aware tie; did not author marked engine10, adapter, c354/kernel or independent marked verifier. Dependency authorship does not supply fresh independent semantic implementation. Whole Source read and raw/AST/compile-only checks; no scientific calls/models/clocks/tests/actuals.",
  "handoff": {
