  "manual_whole_Source_assessment": [
    {
      "finding": "Exact9-field marked flat state maps selected/excluded wrapped keys to freshly rebuilt original keys; c354 validates entire original projection. Independently rebuilt decorated selected packets and full sorted m union plus fixed guard are checked through 9fd6. Extra/absent/assigned0 cannot be silently ignored. No raw/base receipt relabeling.",
      "source_lines": {
        "adapter": [
          72,
          152
        ]
      },
      "topic": "Full marked state and identity"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Every offered original candidate is rebuilt/member-checked, compared whole and required base-legal; every decorated packet is separately rebuilt and independently checked. Ordinary full t/m agreement removes only explicit channel4-conflict candidates, never caught exceptions. Ordered ports and PENDING occupancy=false-fact semantics remain literal.",
      "source_lines": {
        "adapter": [
          174,
          208
        ]
      },
      "topic": "Whole point candidate filtering"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Full c354 proposal checked before new filtering. Complete base cover permits exact filtered0/1/many. Incomplete0/1 is UNKNOWN; two independently valid surviving keys is a lower bound only. New marking/state/binding/query schema prevents copied base evidence from serving as current marked receipt.",
      "source_lines": {
        "adapter": [
          220,
          253
        ],
        "engine": [
          603,
          670
        ]
      },
      "topic": "Complete versus partial degree"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Original complete generator remains unchanged. Filter keeps original survivor order with fresh ordinal and full original provenance; exceptions poison cursor, abort poisons before delegation. EOF untrusted; actual engine certifier freshly gets complete c960+c354 cover, filters and exact-compares full surviving keys. General uncovered EOF remains UNKNOWN. No cap/time/error converts to completion.",
      "source_lines": {
        "adapter": [
          339,
          451
        ],
        "engine": [
          464,
          601
        ]
      },
      "topic": "Filtered fallback order and EOF"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Transition compares literal presence/value at all channel1/4 positions0..row, current output/metadata2/3, local full inventory, t/rootgeneration and current global selected/excluded original+decorated collision ledger. This is a superset of every primitive/decoration support, including unseen candidates. Prior t occupancy only refreshes independently rebuilt known obligation packets. Global ledger change conservatively invalidates; not all-domain-reset by default.",
      "source_lines": {
        "adapter": [
          259,
          336
        ],
        "engine": [
          315,
          427
        ]
      },
      "topic": "Complete unseen possible support"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Fixed guard4,0 has own refcount; selected full globalm adds references. Immutable marking appears in transition authority. COW state/refs/certs/slot archives/observations/reverse/preferences/checkpoints retained, disposable generators reopened and full prefixes replayed. Search finally restores complete owned root and exceptions/UNKNOWN never exclude a child. Monotone work counts/events are not logical rollback state.",
      "source_lines": {
        "engine": [
          176,
          245,
          279,
          391,
          861,
          956
        ]
      },
      "topic": "Guard/refcounts/rollback"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Scheduler function and live decision raw-exact to9; global certified DEAD precedes UNKNOWN/forced/earliestgenBRANCH, ROW/MARK named tie preserved. Both advice callbacks must be None; dormant old advice functions are not supported marked APIs. Exact24 word proposal projects nested original preimage; no proof/activation/current graph or native acceptance.",
      "source_lines": {
        "engine": [
          51,
          83,
          117,
          159,
          619,
          670,
          861,
          956
        ]
      },
      "topic": "Scheduling and disabled advice"
    },
    {
      "finding": "BLOCKER: outer observed ledger checks decorated ID/preimage only. Original base IDs are checked only against selected/excluded and within individual proposal/cursor ledgers. Across separately observed row queries/cursors, equal original IDs with distinct full original preimages are not globally compared. No hash-injectivity assumption is allowed by declared contract. Engine9 originally checked its original keys here; wrapping them must retain that check.",
